cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use chronozarr in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: chronozarr
version: 0.5.1
date-released: 2026-10-24
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/chronozarr/chronozarr"
url: "https://chronozarr.org"
abstract: >-
  chronozarr turns a georeferenced raster time series into an interactive dataset
  that anyone can open with a link. In a web browser, the series plays or scrubs
  like a video. You zoom and pan the map, and a click on a pixel shows its values
  over time. In Python, the same files return the exact numbers you stored. No tile
  server runs anywhere.
keywords:
  - zarr
  - raster
  - time-series
  - remote-sensing
  - earth-observation
  - xarray
authors:
  - family-names: Gearon
    given-names: James H.
    affiliation: University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill
